From 8ecb461363c974966903371c76bc5d54534c4135 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 18:14:02 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 102/104] decode-link: what the links of Marzban and Remnawave
 showed

The decoder was run over the links the generators of the two panels write for a matrix
of inbounds (protocol, transport, security, header type, host settings, flow):

- VMess of Marzban writes the gRPC mode into "type" only when there is one, "none"
  otherwise, and an IPv6 address in brackets: both were refused or kept;
- Hysteria 2 of Remnawave carries the obfuscation, the port hopping and the speeds in
  fm (the finalmask of Xray): they are read from there when the link does not say them
  itself;
- ech as a name and a resolver joined with "+" read as two links glued together,
  the "+" being a space after form decoding;
- the HTTP header of the TCP transport has a list of paths: the first is taken;
- x_padding_bytes of an xhttp link got a warning although it is read;
- fragment and noise, the client's own settings a panel writes into a link, get a
  warning that says so; the WebSocket heartbeat of Xray's client gets none;
- the parameters of TLS in a link without TLS get no warning: the generators write
  them anyway;
- the gRPC authority gets its warning only when it is not what sing-box sends, the
  server name of TLS, and the warning says what follows.
